{
    "_comment": [
        "Row configs for the per-type ACTION detail cards (spec M2.5).",
        "action.html still ships the markup; what lives here is the ORDER and the",
        "identity of each row, so a theme can resequence or drop rows without the",
        "page emitting different markup. `cell` is the class the render function",
        "writes the value into, which is what makes a row addressable at all.",
        "A row with cell:null is one whose markup is not a plain label/value pair",
        "(a spanning header, a nested control); it holds its position and is never",
        "moved, because moving it would separate it from the rows it introduces."
    ],
